json PermitPlace {
    doc """
    The Grand Gaia progression gate -- what the player may enter.  readParam
    @0x13E8E28, dispatch strcmp @0x1392A00, clears its slice with
    removeNormalObjects @0x126C9B0.  11 keys.

    ⚠ DELIBERATELY A STUB -- do not "fix" this into a flat struct.

    The five entity-id keys are MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE DISCRIMINATED VARIANTS, not
    five fields.  Each calls setType with its OWN constant and then setPlaceID,
    so the key that is present IS the entity kind:

        VjCY7rX4 -> type 1  Area     (isArea     @0x126B494 cmp #1)
        MHx05sXt -> type 2  Dungeon  (isDungeon  @0x126B4A4 cmp #2)
        j28VNcUW -> type 3  Mission  (isMission  @0x126B4B4 cmp #3)
        9C64Qwe0 -> type 4  Land     (isLand     @0x126B484 cmp #4)
        0Cq2AlXW -> type 5  Gate     (isGate     @0x126B474 cmp #5)

    readParam is called once per (row, field), so an object carrying all five
    would fire setType/setPlaceID five times and THE LAST KEY WOULD WIN.  One
    entry = exactly one id key.  That is why gimuserver/gme/common/PermitPlace.cpp
    hand-assembles this block as raw JSON and splices it over a "yXNM8kL3":[]
    placeholder instead of serializing a struct.

    The six non-id keys, all optional:
        qY49LBjw setTimeLimit    -- DEFAULTS TO 0, and getRemainingTime
                                    @0x126B548 returns -1 when < 1, so 0 reads as
                                    PERMANENT.  ⚠ OPPOSITE POLARITY to
                                    PermitRecipeInfo::getRemainingTime @0x126D4CC,
                                    where 0 means EXPIRED.
        C1vG0iKh setEnterableFlg -- DEFAULTS TO TRUE (ctor mov w8,#1; strb
                                    [x19,#0x78] @0x126B3BC).  Sending "0" LOCKS
                                    the place; isEnterable @0x126B660 has 35
                                    consumers incl. two isLockDungeon predicates.
                                    ⚠ NEVER lock a KEY-GATED dungeon (a Vortex
                                    parade) to mean "closed".  In
                                    AreaSPSelectScene::touchEnded a locked
                                    dungeon goes to MissionFlgConfirmScene
                                    (+0x848, "Opening Conditions" — it lists
                                    need_mission_id quests only) BEFORE the key
                                    branch at +0xa1c, which reads
                                    getRemainingTime (+0xa68): >= 1 enters, < 1
                                    opens the key prompt (+0xce8).  A closed
                                    parade is enterable with no qY49LBjw.
        s2gM3deu setPeriodText, nA95Bdj6 setQuestBonusType,
        5Z1LNoyH setQuestBonusRate (StrToFloat), 5ry19G4Y setQuestBonusTimeLimit
                                 -- campaign bonus display; we send none, and 0 /
                                    empty correctly reads as "no bonus".

    No accumulation despite re-sending all ~812 entries per UserInfo: readParam
    does removeObject(getType(), getPlaceID()) @0x13E9478 per row before
    addObject, on top of the category sweep.

    Full audit: tools/SERVER_COMPONENT_AUDIT.md.
    """

    field mock type="str" {
      key "INVALID"
      doc "Placeholder so the struct parses.  Nothing populates it -- see the struct doc: this block is hand-assembled in common/PermitPlace.cpp because its entries are discriminated variants."
    }
}

json PermitPlaceML {
    doc """
    The ML slice of the same shared PermitPlaceInfoList.  readParam
    @0x1C6BC54, dispatch strcmp @0x1396C68, clears with removeMLObjects.
    11 keys, same type constants as PermitPlace.

    ⚠ DELIBERATELY A STUB -- do not "fix" this into a flat struct.

    The five entity-id keys are MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE DISCRIMINATED VARIANTS, not
    five fields.  Each calls setType with its OWN constant and then setPlaceID,
    so the key that is present IS the entity kind:

        VjCY7rX4 -> type 1  Area     (isArea     @0x126B494 cmp #1)
        MHx05sXt -> type 2  Dungeon  (isDungeon  @0x126B4A4 cmp #2)
        j28VNcUW -> type 3  Mission  (isMission  @0x126B4B4 cmp #3)
        9C64Qwe0 -> type 4  Land     (isLand     @0x126B484 cmp #4)
        0Cq2AlXW -> type 5  Gate     (isGate     @0x126B474 cmp #5)

    readParam is called once per (row, field), so an object carrying all five
    would fire setType/setPlaceID five times and THE LAST KEY WOULD WIN.  One
    entry = exactly one id key. This slice currently emits no rows.
    common/PermitPlace.cpp builds only the normal yXNM8kL3 slice; adding this
    slice requires its own complete snapshot under the correct outer key.

    The six non-id keys, all optional:
        qY49LBjw setTimeLimit    -- DEFAULTS TO 0, and getRemainingTime
                                    @0x126B548 returns -1 when < 1, so 0 reads as
                                    PERMANENT.  ⚠ OPPOSITE POLARITY to
                                    PermitRecipeInfo::getRemainingTime @0x126D4CC,
                                    where 0 means EXPIRED.
        C1vG0iKh setEnterableFlg -- DEFAULTS TO TRUE (ctor mov w8,#1; strb
                                    [x19,#0x78] @0x126B3BC).  Sending "0" LOCKS
                                    the place; isEnterable @0x126B660 has 35
                                    consumers incl. two isLockDungeon predicates.
        s2gM3deu setPeriodText, nA95Bdj6 setQuestBonusType,
        5Z1LNoyH setQuestBonusRate (StrToFloat), 5ry19G4Y setQuestBonusTimeLimit
                                 -- campaign bonus display; we send none, and 0 /
                                    empty correctly reads as "no bonus".

    No accumulation despite re-sending all ~812 entries per UserInfo: readParam
    does removeObject(getType(), getPlaceID()) @0x13E9478 per row before
    addObject, on top of the category sweep.

    Full audit: tools/SERVER_COMPONENT_AUDIT.md.
    """

    field mock type="str" {
      key "INVALID"
      doc "Placeholder so the struct parses. Nothing currently populates this slice; its entries must be discriminated variants."
    }
}

json PermitPlaceSP {
    doc """
    The SPECIAL (Vortex / Frontier Gate) slice of the same shared
    PermitPlaceInfoList.  readParam @0x13E9538, dispatch strcmp @0x1392A24,
    clears with removeSpecialObjects.  10 keys -- it has NO 0Cq2AlXW (Gate).

    ⚠ AND IT REINTERPRETS ONE KEY: 9C64Qwe0 sets type 1 (Area) here
    @0x13E95B4, not type 4 (Land) as on PermitPlace and PermitPlaceML.
    Same key, three classes, two meanings.

